*.pyc

# The inbox is a staging area; the archive is the operator's own copy of the
# raw broker and firm exports. Neither is published.
#
# The archive stays OUT of the public repository on purpose. It carries the
# firm's own account identifier in the clear, and a track record is a document
# strangers are invited to read closely. Everything a stranger needs to check
# the record — nav.csv, trades.csv, the metrics, the snapshots, the chain — is
# published; the raw exports behind it are held by the operator and can be
# shared with anyone who asks. That is the same line the system this is
# modelled on draws: outputs public, raw broker dumps not.
data/inbox/
data/archive/
data/tpt/
data/publish.log
data/cron.log
